Use the UI"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Restart the DSH Web profile after installing or rebuilding this package, then open **Settings -> Plu"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"gins -> VS Code Themes**. Drop a VSIX onto the import panel or choose it from disk. Every imported V"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"SIX is stored in this browser's IndexedDB; use the saved-package menu to switch between them after a"},{"id":"p14s4","text":" refresh or DSH restart. They are never uploaded. A theme applied through this plugin remains applie"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"d after a refresh; choosing a different DSH theme clears that restoration preference."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"DSH and VS Code have different visual-token systems. The importer maps the workbench palette (backgr"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ounds, text, borders, focus, selection, status colors, and sidebar) into DSH's UI tokens. Syntax tok"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"en colors remain available to the agent parser but do not recolor the DSH interface."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Use from an agent"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Ask the agent to inspect a VSIX, or call the registered tool directly:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Use `detail: \"full\"` to return every resolved color and token rule. The default summary returns meta"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"data, rule counts, inherited files, and the first 24 workbench colors to keep ordinary model context"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"e counts, inherited files, and the first 24 workbench colors to keep ordinary model context compact."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Building and publishing require Node.js 22 or later. The compiled host plugin targets Node.js 20 for"},{"id":"p21s2","text":" DSH runtime compatibility."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
